\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Powers To 26-Month High Against Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 09:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--The Russian ruble powered to a new 26-month high against the dollar Friday, advancing for the third straight day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading corridor earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has appreciated by 4% in the past two weeks and almost 9% since the start of the year against the dollar, buoyed by higher oil prices and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's measures to cut inflation.\par \par \uc2 "We may see some stabilization here," said Nikolay Podguzov, an economist at VTB Capital. "There has been quite a rally and there will be some profit taking."\par \par \uc2 The ruble hit RUB28.11 against the dollar Friday, advancing 0.5% to its strongest level since December 2008. Against a basket of dollars and euros used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to manage fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ruble was down less than 0.1% to RUB33.22.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Russia widened the ruble's trading band against the basket to five rubles earlier this week, with the aim of allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen in order to fight inflation while at the same time making the ruble's movements less predictable to speculators. The ruble's trading band now stands at 32.45-37.45.\par \par \uc2 "As we come near the lower edges of the band, we are likely to see more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Podguzov said, estimating the regulator may purchase up to $400 million in daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  below 33.10.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised rates across the board last week in a bid to control surging inflation, with further rate increases seen as likely.\par \par \uc2 The recent surge in oil prices may provide further support to the ruble in the near term, RBC said, adding that the ruble may hit RUB27.50 against the dollar by the second quarter before weakening slightly later in the year. Oil prices are currently close to two-and-a-half year highs as a result of political turmoil in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 232 9195; ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -0- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 03-04-11 0352ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110304e7340004n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
