\par\par \b \uc2 Russian  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Official: Sees $6B As Maximim  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2010\par 11:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first deputy chairman of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia said Wednesday that he aims to continue moving towards a more flexible exchange rate, which will involve widening the ruble \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor.\par \par \uc2 "Firstly we need to take steps to widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor," Alexey Ulyukayev said during a visit to London.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to delegates at the 17th Russian Banking Forum, organised by Adam Smith Conferences, Ulyukayev defended \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said it is needed to smooth out volatility.\par \par \uc2 But going forward he said there will be less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the size will be smaller, noting the maximum \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be $6 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires, +44 (0) 20 7842 9496;\par \par \uc2 clare.connaghan@dowjones.com [ 01-12-10 1122GMT ]\par \par \uc2 (Adds detail.)\par \par \uc2 By Clare Connaghan\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Russia's first deputy chairman of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia said Wednesday that he aims to continue moving towards a more flexible exchange rate, which will involve widening the ruble \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor.\par \par \uc2 "Firstly we need to take steps to widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor," Alexey Ulyukayev said during a visit to London.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to delegates at the 17th Russian Banking Forum, organised by Adam Smith Conferences, Ulyukayev defended \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said it is needed to smooth out volatility.\par \par \uc2 But going forward he said there will be less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the size will be smaller, noting the maximum \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be $6 billion.\par \par \uc2 When asked if the bank planned to raise interest rates, Ulyukayev said he "cannot say whether hikes were likely or not likely."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left rates unchanged at historic low last week for the sixth consecutive month, saying the economy was still in need of monetary stimulus while inflation risks remained acceptable.\par \par \uc2 But in the text accompanying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision Thursday, it omitted phrasing indicating that interest rates would remain where they are, which had been present in past statements.\par \par \uc2 Russia's refinancing rate stands at 7.75%, an all-time low.\par \par \uc2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires, +44 (0) 20 7842 9496;\par \par \uc2 clare.connaghan@dowjones.com [ 01-12-10 1137GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101201e6c1000xf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
