\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Russia FX interventions \highlight\uc2  to be smaller,less often-c.bank\b0\par\par\uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2010\par 12:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  c.bank plans less frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Deputy c.bank head sees less Dec hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales\par \par \uc2 * C.bank sees no Aussie dollars purchases for minimum 6 mths\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 1 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans less frequent and lower-volume \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in future to let markets set the rouble's exchange rate as much as possible, First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 He stressed however it would not be possible to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  altogether as the bank would need to prevent volatile swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Speaking in Russian at the annual Adam Smith Russian banking forum, Ulyukayev said: "In the near term we will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to iron out volatility but we think they won't be frequent and not in big volumes."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $5 billion in November as the rouble weakened but Ulyukayev said he expected lower sales in December.\par \par \uc2 "It seems to me it will be less in December, the task of repaying debt (by corporates) is over," he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "My feeling is the market will require less volume in future, I think it should be in the region of $4 to $6 billion in future," he added.\par \par \uc2 The rouble's floating corridor was located at 33-37 roubles against the euro-dollar basket, Ulyukayev told Reuters, correcting earlier comments to reporters that put the basket at 35-39 roubles, differing from market estimates. [ID:nLDE6B00XG].\par \par \uc2 Ulyukayev reiterated that the widening of the rouble's floating trading band on Oct. 13 would be followed by further such moves, but gave no details on the possible timing.\par \par \uc2 "We will keep taking steps to keep widening this band in future," Ulyukayev earlier told the conference, noting that the $700 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threshold at which the bank widened the band had been lowered recently to $650 million.\par \par \uc2 "We will keep reducing it so that the exchange rate is determined as far as possible by markets," he added.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has been hit in recent months by capital outflows mostly due to debt repayments. Estimates are for total outflows of around $22 billion this year and Deputy Economy Minister Andrey Klepach said this week outflows could be as high as $25 billion.\par \par \uc2 But Ulyukayev forecast a lower figure, noting the possibility of zero outflows in December. Outflows ran at around $21 billion in the first 10 months of 2010.\par \par \uc2 Russia has the world's third-largest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, of around $490 billion and is diversifying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mix, recently starting purchases of the Canadian dollar.\par \par \uc2 But Ulyukayev said planned purchases of the Australian dollar would not start for another six months at least.\par \par \uc2 "It took us almost a year to start Canadian dollar <CAD=> purchases. At the last \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting we decided to include the Australian dollar in the list of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for reserves," Ulyukayev said.\par \par \uc2 The Russian economy is recovering steadily from the worst recession in 15 years and Ulyukayev forecast banks' loan books to grow by 15-20 percent next year, a figure he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  considered "desirable."\par \par \uc2 "A measured rise is good," he said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Sujata Rao and Carolyn Cohn in London and Elena Fabrichnaya in Moscow; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-CBANK/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|NAT|CANT|AUF|ND|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101201e6c1000qe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
