\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Rouble rebounds on firmer oil, c.bank comments\b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2010\par 10:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Rouble recovers following oil prices\par \par \uc2 * Dealers say c.bank's eases fears of capital outflows\par \par \uc2 * Tax payments period may bolster rouble further\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The rouble firmed on Thursday, boosted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments about smaller than expected capital outflows and a recovery in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  first deputy chairman said he was "surprised" by the rouble's recent weakness, adding that debt-driven capital outflows in the fourth quarter may total $7 billion. [ID:nLDE6AH0WE]\par \par \uc2 Market players, however, were puzzled by the statement, saying that this amount of outflows might had been seen in October alone -- judging from \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account balance and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which totalled $3.2 billion. [ID:nLDE6A713R]\par \par \uc2 "The rouble was supported by the external background and then by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the announced $7 billion of capital outflows can be easily offset by the current account surplus," said Denis Korshilov, chief dealer at Citi in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Russia's current account surplus rose in January-September 2010 to $60.9 billion from $52.2 billion in January-June 2010. [ID:nLDE6950GC]\par \par \uc2 "People who were holding long positions (in dollars and euros) suggested that the demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may fade rapidly," said Viktor Kholoshnoy, a dealer at \uc2 Gazprombank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Citi's Korshilov said such figures imply that the current amount of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $300 million seems excessive, which may push the rouble higher, to the range where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells $150 million a day.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the rouble rate within a floating range against the euro-dollar basket with presumed boundaries at 33.0-37.0 roubles <RUS=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 Dealers say the regulator sells some $300 million a day when the rouble trades at 36.0-36.5 versus the basket and halves \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the range of 35.5-36.0 roubles per basket.\par \par \uc2 The rouble inched up 24 kopecks to 36.07 against the basket on Thursday, hovering some 35 kopecks above its 2010 lows hit in early November.\par \par \uc2 Versus the dollar, the rouble gained 38 kopecks to 30.99 <RUBUTSTN=MCX>. It was up 2 kopecks at 42.31 versus the euro <EURRUBTN=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 Oil, Russia's chief exports, rebounded on Thursday toward $82 per barrel of U.S. crude oil futures [O/R], lending support for the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Closely watching developments in euro zone financials, Russia's market also received some relief as Ireland agreed to work with a European Union-IMF mission on steps to shore up its shattered banking sector. [ID:nLDE6AG004]\par \par \uc2 Russia's upcoming month-end taxes -- which may total at least 550 billion roubles ($17.63 billion) -- may support the rouble as well in coming days, said Dmitry Kharlampiyev, analyst at Petrocommerce bank.\par \par \uc2 He said the nearest target for the rouble's rise lies at 36.0 against the basket, the next target level is 35.70.\par \par \uc2 In the longer-run, the rouble is poised to firm further as Russia pushes on with planned sales of more stakes in major state-controlled companies.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Prime Minister Vladimir Putin approved a plan to sell 1 trillion roubles ($32 billion) in state assets over the next three years to help plug a gap in the budget and lure investors. [ID:nLDE6AG1F1]\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Vladimir Abramov; editing by Patrick Graham and Giles Elgood)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/(UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101118e6bi000ja\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
