\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Russian Ruble Weakens To Year Low Against  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Basket\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2010\par 11:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--The Russian ruble hit its lowest levels of the year against a basket of euros and dollars Wednesday, pressured by foreign debt payments, a lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's increasingly cloudy macroeconomic picture.\par \par \uc2 "There is a significant demand for dollars and euros from importers right now, and not too many sellers," said Selim Agarzayev, a dealer at Metallinvest Bank.\par \par \uc2 The ruble fell 0.7% to as low as 36.09 against the basket, while also losing 1.1% against the dollar to 30.78.\par \par \uc2 Russian corporations must pay off some $36 billion in foreign debt by the end of the year, a factor which has been putting pressure on the ruble as companies sell the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buy dollars and euros.\par \par \uc2 Market participants have also been knocked off balance by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's changes to the floating trading band versus the dollar-euro basket. Last week, the regulator confirmed that it had widened the trading band's borders by one ruble, to 32.80-36.80, in order to allow for greater ruble flexibility.\par \par \uc2 "Now, there is much less certainty about where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step in to support the ruble. People are much less willing to make speculative bets," Agarzayev said.\par \par \uc2 Longer term, the ruble is being pressured by Russia's deteriorating current account surplus, as imports flood the market while the level of exports remains little changed. Imports into the country jumped by 13.3% in August while exports rose by only 0.5%.\par \par \uc2 "People have taken notice of this dynamic and are making their decisions accordingly," said Eugene Belin, head of fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Citi in Russia.\par \par \uc2 -By Ira Iosebashvili, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 232 9195;\par \par \uc2 ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -0- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 20, 2010 05:53 ET (09:53 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020101020e6ak00215\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
