\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Would  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In Ruble On Volatile Oil\b0\par\par\uc2 144 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 10:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0826 GMT [Dow Jones] The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was able to widen its parameters for allowable ruble fluctuations starting Wednesday because the main drivers for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been relatively subdued, but if volatile oil prices were to return, it might have to meddle in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than its current plan suggests, \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2  says. "In the event of higher oil price volatility, it will be hard for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Alfa economist Natalia Orlova says. Ruble strengthens to 35.4180 to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-euro basket, from 35.4798 late yesterday. Ruble strengthens to 29.9236 vs the dollar. (william.mauldin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 14-10-10 0826GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101014e6ae000ro\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
