\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE: Russia Loosens Ruble Policy; No Major Effects Seen\b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2010\par 17:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   (Adds \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  confirmation, market comments) \par  \par   By William Mauldin \par   Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it will start \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to a somewhat lesser degree in the ruble exchange rate starting Wednesday, but traders and analysts said the new policy won't have an immediate effect on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia buys and sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Micex exchange to manage the ruble's exchange rate against a basket of dollars and euros, smoothing out volatility caused by sudden movements in the oil price or local demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the past, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved its floating corridor for the exchange rate by 5 kopeks, or RUB0.05, after buying or selling $700 million to smooth out sudden movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Starting today, it will adjust the corridor when only $650 million is bought or sold, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on its website.\par \par \uc2 More importantly, the width of the floating corridor will also be increased to 4 rubles rather than 3 rubles.\par \par \uc2 The new boundaries for the floating corridor are believed to be at either RUB32.80 or RUB32.90 to the dollar-euro basket on the one side, and RUB 36.80 or RUB36.90 on the other, Renaissance Capital analyst Anton Nikitin said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  analysts said that judging by the last official confirmation of the floating corridor, it may now reach from RUB33.40 to RUB37.40.\par \par \uc2 In either case, the closing level Wednesday of 35.4798 to the basket, recorded before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy announcement, is well within estimates of the floating corridor.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about a change in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, as well as recent data pointing to a sliding trade balance, contributed to ruble weakness Wednesday, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tendency to strengthen or weaken Thursday won't be affected much by the announcement, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The ruble was little changed at 30.1205 against the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been bucking general trends. It has tended to depreciate in recent weeks, even as oil holds steady and other emerging markets struggle to contain higher exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 -By William Mauldin, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 232-9192, william.mauldin@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 13, 2010 11:46 ET (15:46 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020101013e6ad003ta\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
