\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Russia's rouble policy\b0\par\par\uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2010\par 16:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 13 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday widened the rouble's floating corridor against the basket to 4 roubles from 3 -- its first shift in exchange rate policy since the spring.\par \par \uc2 Following are details of current \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. For a story on Wednesday's move, please see [ID:nLDE69C0TW]\par \par \uc2 BASKET <RUS=MCX>\par \par \uc2 Russia introduced a basket for tracking the rouble's course on Feb. 1, 2005, initially made up of 0.1 euros and 0.9 dollars.\par \par \uc2 The euro's share was gradually increased to reach the current 0.45 euros and 0.55 dollars composition on Feb. 8, 2007.\par \par \uc2 WIDE FIXED TRADING BAND\par \par \uc2 In January 2009, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defined the rouble's wide trading band as 26 to 41 roubles. This remains in force and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it has no plans to change it for now.\par \par \uc2 SMALLER FLOATING CORRIDOR WITHIN WIDE BAND\par \par \uc2 Within that set trading band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a 3-rouble-wide floating corridor, whose boundaries are shifted up or down by 5 kopecks for each $700 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at, respectively, the upper or lower boundary.\par \par \uc2 Between mid-February and mid-May 2010 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made 32 such steps, bringing the corridor to 33.40-36.40 roubles against the basket.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday it widened the corridor by 50 kopecks in each direction. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not give the new boundaries, but dealers said they were likely 32.90-36.90.\par \par \uc2 The floating corridor itself is split into three bands. When the rouble is at the weak end of the band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells small volumes of dollars each day. In the middle of the band it does nothing and when the rouble is strong it buys foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not disclose the exact boundaries of the three bands or the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 OUTLOOK\par \par \uc2 The rouble has potential for gains from current levels but they are likely to be capped by demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to rising imports and redemption of foreign debt. More substantial gains now require stronger oil prices, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 A consensus forecast from analysts polled by Reuters late last month [ECILT/RU] shows the rouble at 28.50 per dollar and 33.23 versus the basket in 12 months from, respectively, 30.82 and 33.97 on April 19.\par \par \uc2 MOVE TOWARDS 'DIRTY' FREE FLOAT\par \par \uc2 Russia is gradually moving towards targeting inflation rather than exchange rates and the widening of the corridor is seen as the latest step in that direction.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it is aiming for a managed -- or 'dirty' -- free float and will continue to reserve the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if it deems necessary.\par \par \uc2 Some $500 billion in gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's third largest, give \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The regulator says it already does not target a particular exchange rate, and its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are merely aimed at smoothing out excessive market volatility.\par \par \uc2 Unlike other BRICs, Russia has no capital controls, having resisted calls to reintroduce them during the crisis.\par \par \uc2 (Compiled by Andrey Ostroukh and Toni Vorobyova; Editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101013e6ad0012i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
