\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Russia Loosens Ruble Policy; No Big Effects Seen\b0\par\par\uc2 1,072 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2010\par 18:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1615 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it will start \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to a somewhat lesser degree in the ruble exchange rate starting Wed, but traders and analysts said the new policy won't have an immediate effect on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It will adjust the corridor when only $650 million is bought or sold, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on its website. More importantly, the width of the floating corridor will also be increased to 4 rubles rather than 3 rubles. (william.mauldin@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1554 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys slip more ahead of the 1 p.m. EDT 10-yr sale. The bond market is losing ground to a strong rally in U.S. stocks, golds, crude oils and TIPS. The selling may support demand for the 10-yr sale as the yield is now rising back toward the area of 2.47% considered by some as attractive. 10-yr is 12/32 lower to yield 2.475%. The 30-yr bond is 27/32 lower to yield 3.867%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1551 GMT [Dow Jones] Markit's purchase of a loan messaging system from DTCC will allow the data specialist to better service investors wanting loan portfolio updates on repayments and interest rate changes. DTCC's system was more advanced than Markit's. If an agent bank sends Markit a message, it will be converted to a format for either a website so a lender can see it or to update the lender's portfolio management system, said a Markit spokesman. (katy.burne@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1538 GMT [Dow Jones] Price guidance is out on \uc2 Raytheon Co\uc2 .'s (Baa1/A-) benchmark-sized 3-pt debt offering: 5s at Tsys +60 bps area, 10s at Tsys +80 bps area and 30s at Tsys +110-133 bps range. Joint bookrunners Citi/\uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 /\uc2 UBS\uc2  will lead the pricing which is expected later Weds. Proceeds will be used to fund redemption of notes and for general corporate purposes. (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1538 GMT [Dow Jones] The high-grade corporate market seems a touch skeptical on the ability of the Fed to spur borrowing given its QE2 stance. US bond borrowers have been borrowing less, despite record low rates, according to analysts at \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 . "This is because domestic banks have been deleveraging but the growth in non financial corporate debt has been very modest as well," they said. (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1536 GMT [Dow Jones] As QE2 speculation remains main talking point, fed-funds futures traders pare bets for a funds rate increase next year. Jan 2012 contract prices in only 10% chance of a hike, lower than the 48% chance priced in on Oct. 1. Trading volume light in Jan '12 contract. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1536 GMT [Dow Jones] The Q3 surge in China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by $194.03 billion, the biggest-ever quarterly gain, may usher in tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls despite recent comments promising the opposite, says Capital Economics. That's because a portion of the rise is tied to hot money that was trying to capitalize on the yuan's pace of appreciation versus the dollar in Aug and Sep. "We suspect that the desire to discourage inflows will prompt the Bank to rein in and even reverse the [yuan's] rise against the dollar," after U.S. elections and the G20 summit, said Capital Economics. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1517 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's (JPM) credit-card unit's 3Q performance underscores the sliding revenue trend hitting the card industry as loan balances fall and new rules lower fee income. While the card unit reported a $735M profit, net revenue declined 18% vs year ago to $4.3B. Average card loans fell 17% vs year earlier to $140.1B. Investors should look carefully at the proportion of profits coming from an actual increase in revenue -- a sign of growth -- and the bump in profits from reserve releases as credit trends improve. JPM reduced its reserve for card loan losses by $1.5B. Shares down 0.8% at $40.06. (aparajita.saha-bubna@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1514 GMT [Dow Jones] Center of attention in muni mkt is $1.6 bln NJ Tranportation Trust Fund Auth combination of taxable and tax-exempt bonds with indications of interest on $1.1 bln BABs being taken along with orders on two other series, one being $485 mln of tax-exempts. Not many other sizeable issues on this week's slate, and secondary activity slow. Prices on long end off about 2 BPs, possibly because of further Tsy yield curve steepening. (stan.rosenberg@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1512 GMT [Dow Jones] The move by Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to widen the band it will allow the ruble to trade within against a basket of dollars and euro is a buying opportunity, says Win Thin of BBH. "RUB was the worst performing EMEA \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Q3, and is one of the worst so far in Q4. We do not think this is warranted given the improved global outlook," he said. Thin notes strong economic fundamentals and forecasts rating upgrades by S&P and Fitch to BBB+ over the next 6 to 12 months. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1507 GMT [Dow Jones] Brokerage firms face another full year of reduced earnings as there's no end in sight to Fed's zero interest rate policy. Raymond James, in a morning note, pushes back its prediction for a funds rate increase to January 2012, from its earlier projection of September 2011. "Continuing economic struggles seem to justify our conservatism," the trade note says. Brokerage firms gain from higher rates because they earn interest on the amount of money customers have on deposit. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1506 GMT [Dow Jones] In a banner day for commodity-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , supported by a 1.8% surge for a barrel of oil, AUD/USD reaches 0.9931, the highest level ever hit since the Down Under \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began floating in 1983. Aussie dollar remains a favored \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- and much played one -- with any signs of growth lifting it higher, says Tom Fitzpatrick of Citi.(andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com) [ 10-13-10 1215ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101013e6ad000be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
