\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Rouble hits 3-wk peak vs dlr on taxes, oil\b0\par\par\uc2 737 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2010\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Rouble rises to 3-week high after bout of weakness\par \par \uc2 * Buoyed by month-end tax payments, strong oil prices\par \par \uc2 * Market positioning, uncertainty may curb further gains\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 27 (Reuters) - The rouble hit a three-week high versus the dollar on Monday, extending a recovery from multi-month lows thanks to buying amid ongoing local tax payments, though a sustained appreciation trend looks unlikely.\par \par \uc2 Against the dollar <.DXY>, which was under pressure from several major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rouble rose 27 kopecks, or 0.87 percent to 30.51 <RUBUTSTN=MCX>. This was its strongest level since September 6, heading away from a 10-week low of 31.39 touched two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 "Today's trading day featured the absence of a dollar buyer that has been recently pulling the dollar/rouble pair towards 31.0. Generally, the balance of market powers was biased towards selling (foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 )" said Alexander Panasenko, a dealer at Metallinvestbank.\par \par \uc2 Remaining relatively stable at around 31.0 against the dollar for the last few days, the rouble hit eight-month lows against the euro and the basket last week, bruised by lingering local demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the course of a correction that started late last week, the rouble inched up 19 kopecks, or 0.9 percent to 41.20 versus the euro <EURRUBTN=MCX> after reaching 41.66 on September 23, its lowest since February 2010.\par \par \uc2 Versus the euro-dollar basket, used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to track exchange rates, the rouble rose 24 kopecks, or 0.7 percent to 35.31 <RUS=MCX>, exiting the zone of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and receding from last week's eight-month low of 35.84.\par \par \uc2 Dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the range of 34.40-35.40 roubles against the basket and sells some $150-200 million a day when the rouble slides to the range of 35.40-36.40.\par \par \uc2 "Tax payments and high oil prices are the main factors that favour a stronger rouble," said Alexei Borichev, a dealer at ING bank in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Russia's monthly corporate tax payments usually spur demand for roubles, prompting exporters to convert part of their dollar and euro revenues to meet local liabilities.\par \par \uc2 Natural resource taxes due by Sept. 27 and income taxes due by Sept. 28 could generate up to 360 billion roubles ($11.6 billion) in total, according to Trust bank estimates.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices also comforted the rouble [O/R], with futures for Brent crude rising to almost $79 per barrel <LCOc1>, high enough to generate inflows of dollars into Russia's export-focused economy.\par \par \uc2 CAUTIOUS GAINS AHEAD?\par \par \uc2 Russia's heatwave and drought -- the worst in decades -- hurt the country's harvest and spurred a rise in imports that boosted inflation and undermined growth to put downward pressure on the rouble in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to shed light on the drought's implications in the accompanying statement for the board meeting while keeping interest rates unchanged at record lows. [ID:nLDE68N1FQ]\par \par \uc2 Dealers say the market reaction to keeping rates on hold will be negligible as such a decision is already priced in and the rouble is likely to remain volatile but still at a long distance from recent multi-month lows.\par \par \uc2 "The rouble has a chance to inch up but I think it is premature to speak of a new trend of appreciation", said Panasenko at Metallinvestbank.\par \par \uc2 Any further rise in the rouble against the basket will face resistance, especially at levels close to 35.20 per basket where players had been opening short positions in the basket and now may use any rouble rise as a chance to square these positions, said a dealer at a Russian bank in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 While the short-term outlook remains murky for the rouble, its longer run potential looks positive due to Russia's sound fundamentals, supported by strong oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Technical analysis points to more potential downside for the rouble, although analysts believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism and \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account surplus will keep this in check. [ID:nLDE68N09T] (Additional reporting by Dmitry Antonov; editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/(UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|E|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100927e69r000jj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
