\par\par \b \uc2 Russia cbank bought $1.1 bln and 136 mln euros in Aug\b0\par\par\uc2 156 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2010\par 14:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 7 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it bought $1.1 billion and 135.6 million euros in August on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in "target" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  compared to $0.46 billion and 29 million euros in July.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the MICEX exchange to offset upward pressure on the rouble <RUB=>, considering the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the basis of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account and oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Keeping the rouble within a floating range of 33.40-36.40 against the euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX>, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys some $100-150 million a day in the range of 33.40-34.40, dealers say. The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures are broadly in line with this assumption. (Writing by Andrey Ostroukh; Editing by Toni Vorobyova)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-CBANK/ (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100907e697000ra\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
