\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian rouble rallies on strong oil, more gains seen\b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2010\par 08:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2  * Rouble hits three-month high of 29.67 vs dollar\par \par \uc2  * Touches two-month peak vs basket at 34.00\par \par \uc2  * Underpinned by stronger oil, position squaring\par \par \uc2  * More speculative gains possible\par \par \uc2    (Adds quotes, details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Aug 3 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble jumped to multi-month peaks on Tuesday, showing increased correlation with oil prices that soared above $81 per barrel, and dealers say further speculative gains look possible.\par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the rouble closed up 37 kopecks, or 1.24 percent at 29.73 <RUBUTSTN=MCX>, breaking through the psychologically key 30 mark for the first time since early May.\par \par \uc2  Moving deeper into the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  zone,  the rouble hit its highest since May 31 against the euro-dollar basket of 34.00 <RUS=MCX>. It closed up 24 kopecks or 0.7 percent at 34.05 versus the basket, used by the regulator to track exchange rates.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains so-called "target" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying some $150 million a day in the range of 33.40-34.40 roubles per basket, to ease upward pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers say.\par \par \uc2  But on Tuesday such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no evident impact on the rouble as they were fully offset by the effect of oil prices, which rallied above $81 per barrel [O/R] amid broader dollar weakness and expectations of falling U.S. inventories.\par \par \uc2  According to Reuters data, the correlation between oil prices and the rouble has been increasing for the last few weeks and is the highest since early June. [ID:nLDE6720SF]\par \par \uc2  "We saw a squaring of long positions (in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) by foreigners and big local banks," said Sergei Fishgoit, a dealer at Otrkitiye bank.\par \par \uc2  "Today we've passed an important level for non-residents of 34.10 (roubles per basket) and I don't exclude a further firming in the rouble as soon as tomorrow," he said. Non-residents tend to look at technical levels more than domestic investors.\par \par \uc2   The rouble gains were also seen on the forward market, with the six-month dollar/rouble non-deliverable forward (NDF) implied yield falling to a one-month low of 3.3 percent.\par \par \uc2  "Amid a weaker basket, non-residents and major domestic banks were selling the curve (NDFs for the dollar/rouble)," said Alexei Kulakov, a forward trader at \uc2 Promsvyazbank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Currently, technical analysis points to rouble resistance at 34.00 per basket and a breakthrough would mean a further possible upside move to 33.75, Petrocommerce bank said. [ID:nLDE672158]  (Editing by Susan Fenton) \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/(UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100803e683000gh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
