\par\par \b \uc2 Russia cbank bought $1.7 bln, 417 mln euros in June\b0\par\par\uc2 153 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2010\par 15:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, July 7 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $1.66 billion and 417 million euros ($559.5 million) in so-called target \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June in a bid to lessen the impact of oil price moves on the rouble, data showed on Wednesday. The regulator buys foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rouble trades in the 33.30-34.30 range against the basket, purchasing several hundred million dollars a day.\par \par \uc2 The rouble spent around 10 days weaker than that level in June, meaning the purchases were lower than those in May. The volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in line with expectations.\par \par \uc2 For a detailed explanation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, please see Reuters' interview with first deputy chairman Alexei Ulyukayev on [ID:nLDE65O03B]. (Writing by Toni Vorobyova, editing by Mike Peacock)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ROUBLE/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100707e677000vo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
