\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian rouble up slightly, market eyes oil\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2010\par 16:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Minor gains vs euro, basket\par \par \uc2 * Trading activity subdued due to U.S. holiday\par \par \uc2 * Oil above current levels to take rouble higher - dealers\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, July 5 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble showed modest gains versus the euro and its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in light trade on Monday, supported by stable oil prices and with the market eyeing commodities for clues as to future moves.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro-dollar basket, the rouble was up 2 kopecks at 34.70 <RUS=MCX>, staying 12 kopecks off a five-week low hit last Friday.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices -- the rouble's main benchmark -- stabilised on Monday above three-week lows at levels above $72 per barrel [O/R], which are supportive for the rouble as they ensure Russia maintains a current account surplus.\par \par \uc2 On the global \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the euro <EUR=> was steady.\par \par \uc2 "Oil stands still, the euro stands still. So the rouble doesn't head anywhere," said Roman Pakhomenko, dealer at Lanta bank.\par \par \uc2 Investors were also reluctant to take new positions due to the Independence Day holiday in the U.S., dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Versus the dollar, the rouble shed 6 kopecks to 31.16 <RUBUTSTN=MCX> but it gained 10 kopecks against the euro to 39.05 <EURRUBTN=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 Further moves in the rouble will depend mainly on commodity prices, dealers said, noting that the last time the rouble had been trading at similar levels, oil prices were below $70 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 "If oil continues sliding, it will make sense betting on the stronger basket towards the area of 35.0 roubles," said Viktor Anisimov, a dealer at Alba Alliance.\par \par \uc2 Consolidation of crude oil prices at current levels, or an increase, will provide the rouble with the potential to recover back to levels of 34.40 against the basket pretty soon, said Pakhomenko at Lanta.\par \par \uc2 Dealers are eyeing 34.40 because \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is entering the market with targeted \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the range of 33.40-34.40, buying several hundred millions of dollars a day to absorb capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Keeping the rouble within a floating corridor of 33.40-36.40, the regulator is expected to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the range of 35.40-36.40 and does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the middle area of 34.40-35.40.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh; editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100705e675000u6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
