\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING:ECB's Makuch; Russian, Polish Data Eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 By Leos Rousek   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 1,204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2010\par 05:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par Local/GMT \par  \par 1130/0930 Hungary 3-month T-bill tender \par 1300/1100 ECB board member and Slovak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Jozef Makuch at \par           press conference on Slovak economic outlook \par 1400/1200 Poland May CPI, seen at +2.4% on year \par NA/NA     Russian May industrial output data. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Dow Jones)--Key economic data from Poland and Russia, along with the Slovakian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economic projections take center stage Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Jozef Makuch, the media-shy European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy maker and governor of Slovakis's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will present the bank's economic forecasts for 2010 and 2011. Since his appointment to the ECB's governing board in January, Makuch has largely stayed away from the media limelight.\par \par \uc2 In Warsaw, May inflation data will be in focus. Economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires expect inflation to have remained unchanged from April, due to stubbornly high fuel and food prices. Bank Pekao said in a research note that the same factors pose upside risks for inflation in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Russia's industrial output figures for May will be keenly watched as investors hope for follow through on data for April, when manufacturing growth hit a four-year high and indicated that government policies to stimulate the economy may be finally working.\par \par \uc2 In Prague, ongoing coalition-building talks remain in focus, with expectations that President Vaclav Klaus may formally appoint Petr Necas, the leader of conservative Civic Democrats, as prime minister-designate later this week.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                    2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 25.5400-00 25.5870-70 -0.18  25.6080 25.5600  -3.22 \par EUR/HUF 278.91-41  278.85-36  +0.02  279.04  279.31   +3.08 \par EUR/PLN 4.0753-03  4.0747-98  +0.01  4.0770  4.0785   -0.74 \par USD/RUB 31.658-63  31.658-63   0.00  Untraded today   +4.44 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint may weaken further against the euro, a trader said, adding that investors are wary of moving into Hungarian assets in the wake of recent negative comments from the new government. Two weeks ago, comments from government officials comparing Hungary's economic situation to that of Greece, sent Hungarian and regional assets tumbling.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish zloty is expected to continue strengthening toward PLN4.05 against the euro amid demand from foreign banks in an environment where liquidity is relatively low, a trader said. Tuesday's CPI release for May shouldn't impact the zloty, even though the headline figure is likely to be higher than the annual 2.1% rate estimated by the finance ministry, the trader added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Czech koruna may test levels at CZK25.600 against the euro Tuesday, having broken resistance at 25.65 Monday, a local trader said. Any news on the completion of post-election talks may also support the koruna, the trader added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par    HUNGARIAN BOND YIELDS - The three-year bond yield was at 6.82& Monday afternoon from 6.86% late Friday. The five-year was at 7.25% from 7.27%, the 10-year was at 7.45% from 7.50%. \par  \par    POLISH BOND YIELDS - The average yield of two-year bonds was flat Monday afternoon at 4.55% versus late Friday, five-year was at 5.22% from 5.28%, and ten-year at 5.74% from 5.77%. \par  \par    CZECH BOND YIELD - The yield on the benchmark 10-year paper was unchanged on the day late Monday at 4.08%. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian bond market is expected to stay muted until Thursday, when the state debt agency holds its next government bond auction. Markets expect relatively low demand, which could put pressure on bond prices in the secondary market, a trader said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Polish bond yields are expected to decline further, until Wednesday's planned PLN1.5 billion to PLN3 billion auction of 10-year bonds, which will be a vital test of market demand, a trader said. He noted that in the meanwhile, sentiment remains positive, thanks to a stronger zloty.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par STOCKS \par WIG20                    2403.9  gain   25.5  up 1.1% \par BUX                     21472.7  gain  195.2  up 0.9% \par PX                       1153.3  gain    7.8  up 0.7% \par RTS                            markets closed \par MICEX                          markets closed \par Stoxx EU Enlarged        2221.3  gain 14.6    up 0.7% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN WARSAW: Tuesday may bring a minor downward correction of the WIG20, as demand remains relatively weak. Volatility set to continue, a trader said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN PRAGUE: Investors will likely tread carefully Tuesday but some Czech blue chips, namely New World Resources, banking stocks and CEZ, may find enough demand to rise slightly, one local trader said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN BUDAPEST: Paltry volumes Monday suggest that peices may fall Tuesday, an Erste bank trader said. MOL will be in focus in the wake of the news that the Hungarian government wants the buy Russian oil firm, Surgutneftegas's stake in the company, the trader added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Leos Rousek, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 420 222 315 290; leos.rousek@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Margit Feher in Budapest, Malgorzata Halaba and Marcin Sobczyk in Warsaw, and Ira Iosebashvili in Moscow contributed to the briefing.) [ 06-14-10 2354ET ]\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Eyes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  In Kyrgyzstan \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW (AFP)--A Russian-led security group doesn't rule out military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Kyrgyzstan to bring ethnic violence there under control, a senior Russian official was quoted as saying Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Hungary Favors Change In EU Regulations On Private Pension Funds \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--Hungary supports a possible change to European Union regulations on private pension fund systems as that would significantly narrow Hungary's budget deficit and lower public debt, Hungarian Economy Minister Gyorgy Matolcsy said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China-Russia Crude Pipeline \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  End-October -Xinhua \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--\f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., China's largest oil and gas producer, has said that a China-Russian crude oil pipeline is due to be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Oct. 31, the state-controlled Xinhua news agency reported late Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Audi To Cease Production In Russia Later This Year -Vedomosti \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Audi AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NSU.XE) will stop assembling cars in Russia this year, business daily Vedomosti quotes a local representative of the German luxury auto maker as saying in Tuesday's edition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Hungary In Talks To Buy Russian Surgut's Stake In MOL -Agency \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The Hungarian government is in talks with Surgutneftegas (SNGS.RS) about buying the Russian oil company's 21.2% stake in Hungarian oil and gas firm MOL Nyrt. (MOL.BU), state news agency MTI reports Monday, citing Hungary's Development Minister Tamas Fellegi.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AES To Acquire Wind-Power Pipeline In Poland \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AES Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s (AES) wind-generation business agreed to acquire a wind-development pipeline in Poland, boosting its planned megawattage in the country by more than four-fifths.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Poland Plans To Hand Over Israeli "Agent" To Germany-Report \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW (AFP)--Polish prosecutors Monday said they aimed to hand over to Germany an Israeli suspected of being a Mossad agent linked to the January killing of a Hamas chief, despite Israel's calls for him to go home. [ 06-15-10 0000ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100615e66f0002k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
