\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian rouble ends down on risk aversion\b0\par\par\uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2010\par 09:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Rouble volatile, ends week down\par \par \uc2 * Hit by risk aversion and U.S. payrolls\par \par \uc2 * Some recovery possible, volatility to remain\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, recasts with weekly results)\par \par \uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, June 4 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble fell on Friday to finish lower on the week as it was pressured by rising risk aversion and was not helped by a pull-back in oil prices after disappointing U.S. employment data.\par \par \uc2 Talk of a "Greek-style" debt crisis in Hungary [ID:LDE65306M] raised risk aversion in global markets on Friday, helping pressure the rouble which lost 12 kopecks, or 0.3 percent to 34.32 versus the euro-dollar basket and fell 38 kopecks, or 1.2 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile oil prices, the rouble's main driver, pulled back after a weaker-than-expected U.S. jobs report [ID:nOAT004640]. However, analysts said oil prices remain generally supportive for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels still above $70 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 On the week, which saw Russia cut interest rates on Monday, the rouble lost 37 kopecks, or 1.1 percent to 34.31 against the euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX> -- used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to track \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves -- heading away from a 17-month high of 33.40 hit in mid-May.\par \par \uc2 Against the broadly stronger dollar <RUBUTSTN=MCX>, the rouble lost 75 kopecks, or 2.3 percent on the week, sliding to 31.42 which is 27 kopecks above its 2010 low of 31.68 touched last week.\par \par \uc2 Although persistent worries about the fiscal health of countries in Europe bruised the rouble, they also helped it to a slight 0.2 percent gain on the week versus the euro to 37.85 <EURRUBTN=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 VOLATILE TRADE\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a session low of 34.35 versus the basket from a peak of 34.03 on the MICEX exchange. However, dealers said it was premature to speak of a rapid depreciation. "We don't see distinct flows, the rouble becomes more volatile. I don't think one should be afraid of devaluation moves but the dollar may rise higher," said Mikhail Anisimov, chief dealer at VTB Capital.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also continued to add pressure by maintaining its so-called "planned" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , purchasing around $300 million a day to absorb inflows of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the current account surplus, dealers say.\par \par \uc2 After the market close on Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first deputy chairman Alexei Ulyukayev said the regulator may consider reducing the size of planned \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  following a fall in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade surplus. [ID:nLDE6531FG]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could recover next week as bad news this week has been priced in and as oil prices are expected to stay above $70 a barrel, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 In the weeks ahead, domestic factors are likely to come into play, they said.\par \par \uc2 "The first important thing is whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will reduce its purchases (\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). Apparently, it will. The second important thing is how RUSAL will set its debts", said Viktor Kholoshnoy, dealer at \uc2 Gazprombank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The world's top aluminium producer RUSAL > faces a loan redemption to the amount of $4.5 billion, with Russian banks VEB and \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  most likely to refinance the loan. [ID:nLDE6530OX]\par \par \uc2 "If RUSAL or banks buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to repay the debt, it may bury the rouble's correlation with oil prices," Kholoshnoy said. (Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100604e664000hv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
