\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russia cbank buys $11.3 bln, 412 mln euros in April\b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2010\par 14:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Buys $11.34 billion and 412 million euros in April\par \par \uc2 * "Planned" purchases at $4.17 billion and 170 million euros\par \par \uc2 * Suggests rise in daily planned \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as expected\par \par \uc2 (Adds background)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had bought $11.34 billion and 412 million euros ($552.8 million) in April in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at slowing down the rouble's oil-fuelled appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The data confirmed that the regulator slightly increased so-called daily planned purchases last month. But it stuck by its policy of keeping the rouble within a floating band against a euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX> and shifting the corridor by 5 kopecks for each $700 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its boundary.\par \par \uc2 It made 10 such shifts in April, implying $7 billion of boundary \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers have estimated -- a figure in line with the official \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data released on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carries out so-called "planned" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the band. The planned purchases totalled $4.17 billion and 170 million euros in April -- up from $3.06 billion and 174 million euros the previous month.\par \par \uc2 That translates into around $200 million of planned \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  per day in April and backs dealers' theory that the size of such purchases had been increased. In March, planned \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  averaged around $150 million a day.\par \par \uc2 For the fourth month in a row there were no foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, reflecting a broad appreciation trend in the rouble fanned by high oil prices, a domestic economic recovery and relatively high yields.\par \par \uc2 In March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $14.48 billion and 443 million euros, with the higher volume of total \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflecting the bigger rally in the rouble seen that month. (Writing by Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ROUBLE/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100507e657001hs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw90\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1350\pichgoal600
