Federation, or \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia (Rossiya), is a sovereign and democratic\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              federal state, consisting of \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 83 sub-federal political units, referred to as\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              "Federation subjects." Russia \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 is the largest country in the world by land\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              mass, covering 17.1 million \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 square kilometres, approximately one-eighth of\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              the Earth's land area. Russia \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 borders 16 countries and spans nine time\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              zones, extending some 9,000 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 kilometres from the Baltic Sea in the west to\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              the Pacific Ocean in the east \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and some 4,000 kilometres from its southern\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              border on the Black and \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Caspian Seas to its northern limits on the Arctic\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              Ocean.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bonds\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Title                                        U.S.$2,000,000,000 3.625 per \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 cent. Bonds due 2015 and U.S. $3,500,000,000\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              5.00 per cent. Bonds due 2020.\par Interest                                     The 2015 Bonds bear interest \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from 29 April 2010 at 3.625 per cent. per\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              annum, payable semi-annually \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in arrear on 29 April and 29 October in each\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              year, commencing on 29 October \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              The 2020 Bonds bear interest \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from 29 April 2010 at 5.00 per cent. per\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              annum, payable semi-annually \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in arrear on 29 April and 29 October in each\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              year, commencing on 29 October \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Redemption                                   Unless previously redeemed, or\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 purchased and cancelled, each 2015 Bond will\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              be redeemed at its principal \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 amount on 29 April 2015 subject as provided in\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              Condition 7.\par                                              Unless previously redeemed, or \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 purchased and cancelled, each 2020 Bond will\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              be redeemed at its principal \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 amount on 29 April 2020 subject as provided in\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              Condition 7.\par Repurchase                                   The Russian Federation may at\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 any time purchase Bonds in the open market or\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              otherwise at any price. Any \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bonds so purchased may be cancelled or held and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              resold.\par Status                                       Each of the 2015 Bonds and the\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2020 Bonds constitute direct, unconditional,\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              unsecured and unsubordinated \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 obligations of the Russian Federation and rank\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              pari passu without any \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 preference among themselves and pari passu in all\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              respects with all other \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 present and future unsecured and unsubordinated\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              obligations of the Russian \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Events of Default                            (1) Failure to pay any amount\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of principal or interest in respect of the\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              2015 Bonds or the 2020 Bonds, \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 as applicable, when due and such failure\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              continues for a period of 30 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 calendar days.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              (2) Failure to perform or \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 comply with any obligation in respect of the 2015\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              Bonds or the 2020 Bonds, as \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 applicable, which default (if capable of\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                              remedy) is not remedied within\par                                                                             \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 60 days after written notice from any\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bondholder (as defined in Condition\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1(b)).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (3) The acceleration of the maturity\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of any Public External Indebtedness\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (as defined in Condition 4(c)), any\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 failure to pay the final instalment of\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 principal in respect of any Public\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 External Indebtedness following the\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expiration of any applicable grace\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 period, or the acceleration of any\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                             obligation under a guarantee\par                                                                             constituting Public External\par                                                                            \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indebtedness or the failure to pay the\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 final instalment of principal in\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 respect of any such guaranteed\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 obligation following the expiration of\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 any applicable grace period, and such\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 guarantee is not honoured; provided\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that the aggregate amount of the\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 relevant Public External Indebtedness\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 equals or exceeds U.S. $75,000,000 (or\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its equivalent in any other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (4) The Russian Federation declares a\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 moratorium on the payment of principal\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of or interest on any part of its\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Public External Indebtedness.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (5) The Russian Federation or any\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 agency or entity acting on behalf of\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Russian Federation contests the\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 validity of the 2015 Bonds or the 2020\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bonds, as applicable, or denies any of\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Russian Federation's obligations\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 under such Bonds or it is or becomes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 unlawful for the Russian Fede