 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (4) Excludes interbudgetary transfers to state extra-budgetary funds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Source: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Government's initial macroeconomic assumptions for 2010 included: an average price per barrel of Urals oil of U.S. $58, overall nominal GDP growth of 10.7% and annual inflation of 10%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par The 2010 Budget Law envisages revenue in 2010 of 6,950 billion\par roubles (including 3,194 billion roubles of oil and gas revenues), or 16.1% of\par GDP. This revenue estimate assumes value added taxes on domestically produced\par and imported goods and services equal to 5.1% of GDP, profit taxes equal to\par 0.5% of GDP, excise taxes equal to 0.4% of GDP, natural resources extraction\par taxes equal to 2.6% of GDP and non-tax revenue (including customs duties)\par equal to 7.5% of GDP. Total expenditure for 2010 is budgeted to be 9,887\par billion roubles, or 22.9% of GDP, with debt service costs accounting for 0.7%\par of GDP.\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The 2010 Budget Law provides for a fiscal deficit in 2010 of 2,937.0 billion roubles, or 6.8% of GDP, and a primary deficit of 2,633 billion roubles, or 6.1% of GDP. The Government intends to seek new external budget financing in 2010 of 429.6 billion roubles, or 1.0% of GDP, and domestic borrowings of 2,507.3 billion roubles, or 5.8% of GDP.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In accordance with the 2010 Budget Law, the Reserve Fund is not expected to generate receipts in 2010-2012 and thus is expected to be substantially depleted during this period. It is anticipated that revenues of the National Welfare Fund will decline by approximately 60% between the beginning of 2010 and the end of 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In 2011 and 2012, the Government expects to finance the federal deficit with a combination of external and domestic borrowing as well as with proceeds from the Reserve Fund.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Budget Revenue\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table sets forth information regarding federal budget revenue for the years 2005 to 2009:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par                             Federal Budget Revenue\par \par                                                           2005         2006         2007         2008         2009\par \par                                                                            (millions of roubles)\par \par Total Revenue                                            5,127,229    6,278,888    7,781,119    9,275,931    7,336,773\par Total revenue net of UST                                 4,859,714    5,963,050    7,376,139    8,769,163    6,826,998\par Tax revenue                                              3,130,247    3,595,656    4,633,704    5,232,654    3,896,499\par Profit taxes                                               377,591      509,913      641,322      761,129      195,420\par VAT                                                      1,472,211    1,510,904    2,261,477    2,132,203    2,049,964\par Domestic VAT                                             1,025,668      924,190    1,390,390      998,388    1,176,608\par Import VAT                                                 446,543      586,714      871,087    1,133,815      873,356\par Excise taxes                                               107,192      110,488      135,035      160,491      101,542\par Natural resources taxes                                    872,310    1,116,685    1,157,362    1,637,515    1,006,261\par UST transfer to the federal budget                         267,515      315,838      404,980      506,768      509,775\par Other tax revenue                                           33,428       31,828       33,529       34,547       33,537\par Non-tax revenue                                          1,996,982    2,683,232    3,147,415    4,043,277    3,440,274\par Customs duties           