 reliance on\par Regulation S. Terms used in this paragraph have the respective meanings given\par to them by Regulation S. The Bonds are being offered and sold outside of the\par United States in reliance on Regulation S. The State Contract provides that\par the Managers may, through their respective U.S. affiliates, resell a portion\par of the Bonds within the United States only to qualified institutional buyers\par in reliance on Rule 144A. In addition, until 40 days after the commencement of\par the offering, an offer or sale of Bonds within the United States by any dealer\par (whether or not it is participating in the offering) may violate the\par registration requirements of the Securities Act if such offer is made\par otherwise than in accordance with Rule 144A.\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 United Kingdom\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par Each Manager has severally and not jointly, nor jointly and\par severally, represented and agreed that it has complied and will comply with\par all applicable provisions of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 with\par respect to anything done by it in relation to the Bonds in, from or otherwise\par involving the United Kingdom.\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par Each Manager has severally and not jointly, nor jointly and\par severally, represented and agreed that it will, to the best of its knowledge\par and belief, comply in all material respects with all applicable securities\par laws and regulations in each jurisdiction in which it purchases, offers, sells\par or delivers Bonds or has in its possession or distributes the Prospectus or\par any other offering material.\par \par Each purchaser of Bonds must comply with all applicable laws and\par regulations in force in any jurisdiction in which it purchases, offers or\par sells Bonds or possesses or distributes this Prospectus or any part of it and\par must obtain any consent, approval or permission required by it for the\par purchase, offer or sale by it of Bonds under the laws and regulations in force\par in any jurisdiction to which it is subject or in which it makes such\par purchases, offers or sales and neither the Issuer nor any Manager shall have\par any responsibility therefor.\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some of the Managers, dealers and agents who participate in the securities distribution may engage in other transactions with, or perform other services for, the Issuer in the ordinary course of business, for which they have received or will continue to receive customary compensation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par                              GENERAL INFORMATION\par \par 1. The Bonds will be accepted for clearance through DTC, Euroclear\par and Clearstream. The CUSIP numbers, ISIN numbers and Common Codes of the Bonds\par are as follows:\par \par 2015 Bonds\par \par                                                                          Restricted Global    Unrestricted\par                                                                                 Bond          Global Bond\par \par CUSIP                                                                            78307A DA8       X74344 DN3\par ISIN                                                                           US78307ADA88     XS0504954180\par Common Code                                                                       050574679        050495418\par 2020 Bonds\par \par                                                                           Restricted Global   Unrestricted\par                                                                                 Bond          Global Bond\par \par CUSIP                                                                            78307A DB6       X74344 DP8\par ISIN                                                                           US78307ADB61     XS0504954347\par Common Code                                                                       050574695        050495434\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2. The listing of the Bonds on the Official List will be expressed in dollars as a percentage of their principal amount (excluding accrued interest). Transactions will normally be effected for settlement in dollars and, under current practice, for delivery on the fifth business day after the day of the transaction.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is expected that listing on the Official List and admission of the Bonds to trading on the Market will be granted on or about 30 April 2010, subject only to the issue of the Bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par If the Bonds are not issued as mentioned in this document, the\par listing and admission to trading of the Bonds may be cancelled. Prior to\par official listing and admission to trading, however, dealings in the Bonds will\par be permitted by the London Stock Exchange  in accordance with its rules. All\par reasonable efforts will be used to maintain any such listing and admission to\par trading of the Bonds for so long as any of the Bonds remain outstanding.\par \par For 12 months starting on the date this Prospectus is made\par available, the following documents (with English translations where necessary)\par may be inspected during normal business hours (local time) on any weekday\par (Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays excluded) at the office of the Paying\par Agent, namely:\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The Fiscal Agency Agreements, which include the forms of the Global Bonds and the Bond Certificates; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The authorisations referred to in item 4 below.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This Prospectus is available free of charge on the website of the London Stock Exchange , being \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.londonstockexchange.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.londonstockexchange.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Copies of Russia's Federal Budget are available free of charge on the website of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Russian Federation ( \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.minfin.ru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.minfin.ru }}}\uc2 \f2 ).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Issuer does not publish financial accounts audited by non-State entities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3. The Russian Federation will obtain prior to the Closing Date all necessary consents, approvals and authorisations in the Russian Federation in connection with the issue of, and performance of its obligations under, the Bonds and the Fiscal Agency Agreements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par 4. The issue of the Bonds and the execution of the Fiscal Agency\par Agreements were authorised pursuant to Federal Law No. 136-FZ of 29 July 1998\par (as amended) "On the Specifics of Issuance and Circulation of State and\par Municipal Securities;" Federal Law No. 308-FZ of 2 December 2009 (as amended)\par "On the Federal Budget for 2010 and 2011-2012 (forecast);" Resolution of the\par Government of the Russian Federation dated 8 April 2010 No. 509-r; Resolution\par of the Government of the Russian Federation dated 8 April 2010 No. 217; Order\par of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dated 15 April 2010 No. 31n;\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Order of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dated 23 April 2010 No. 243; and Order of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dated 23 April 2010 No. 244.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par 5. Article 1210 of the Civil Code provides that the parties to an\par agreement may choose the governing law of the agreement, except that, if the\par agreement relates solely to one jurisdiction, a Russian court is entitled to\par apply the law of such jurisdiction. Therefore, the choice of English law will\par govern rights and obligations in respect of the Bonds in the case of any Bonds\par held by a foreign person. However, it is uncertain whether the choice of\par English law to govern rights and obligations in respect of the Bonds would be\par given effect by a court of the Russian Federation in the case of Bonds held by\par a Russian person.\par \par 6. Under current Russian law, a state duty may be payable upon the\par initiation of any action or proceeding arising out of the Bonds in any court\par of the Russian Federation. Such duty, which shall not exceed the maximum value\par for duties under Russian law, is based on formulas under Russian law that take\par into account the amount of the relevant claim.\par \par 7. The Russian Federation is a sovereign state and has not waived\par any rights to sovereign immunity it may have in any jurisdiction. Accordingly,\par the Russian Federation may be entitled to immunity from suit in any action or\par proceeding arising out of the Bonds, and the Russian Federation and its\par assets, properties and revenues may be entitled to immunity in any enforcement\par action. The Russian Federation has also not submitted to the jurisdiction of\par any court, agreed that any disputes may be resolved in any forum or appointed\par any agent for service of process in any jurisdiction in connection with any\par action or proceeding arising out of the Bonds. It may consequently be\par difficult for an investor to obtain a judgment against the Russian Federation\par in a foreign court.\par \par 8. A final judgment rendered by a foreign court will generally be\par recognised and enforced in the Russian Federation if there is an international\par treaty in effect between the Russian Federation and the country where the\par judgment is rendered providing for the mutual recognition and enforcement of\par judgments. There are no international treaties in effect today providing for\par the mutual recognition and enforcement of foreign judgments rendered by courts\par in the Russian Federation and courts in most of the countries where Bond\par investors are likely to reside, including the United States and the United\par Kingdom.\par \par In the absence of an applicable treaty, enforcement of a final\par judgment rendered by a foreign court may still be recognised by a Russian\par court on the basis of reciprocity, if courts of the country where the foreign\par judgment is rendered have previously enforced judgments issued by Russian\par courts. While Russian courts have recently recognised and enforced English and\par Dutch court judgments on these grounds, the existence of reciprocity must be\par established at the time the recognition and enforcement of a foreign judgment\par is sought, and it is not possible to predict whether a Russian court will in\par the future recognise and enforce on the basis of reciprocity a judgment issued\par by a foreign court, including an English or Dutch court.\par \par Even if an applicable international treaty is in effect or a\par foreign judgment might otherwise be recognised and enforced on the basis of\par reciprocity, the recognition and enforcement of a foreign judgment will in all\par events be subject to exceptions and limitations provided for in Russian law.\par For example, a Russian court may refuse to recognise or enforce a foreign\par judgment if its recognition or enforcement would contradict Russian public\par policy.\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As a result, it may be difficult to obtain recognition or enforcement in the Russian Federation of a foreign judgment in respect of the Bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par 9. During the previous 12 months, the Russian Federation has been\par involved in a number of litigation and arbitration proceedings in which\par substantial claims have been asserted or substantial damages sought against\par the Russian Federation. The Russian Federation does not believe, however, that\par any pending litigation or arbitration proceeding involving the Russian\par Federation, or any threatened litigation or arbitration proceeding of which\par the Russian Federation is aware, has had or will have a significant effect on\par the financial position of the Russian Federation.\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10. Since 31 December 2009, there have been no significant changes relating to the tax and budgetary systems, gross public debt, foreign trade and balance of payment figures, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, financial position and resources and income and expenditure figures of the Issuer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11. The business address of the Issuer is 9 Ilyinka Street, Moscow 109097, Russia, and its telephone number is +7 495 913 4653.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                     ISSUER\par \par                               Russian Federation\par               c/o \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Russian Federation\par                                9 Ilyinka Street\par                                 Moscow 103097\par                               Russian Federation\par \par                   JOINT LEAD MANAGERS AND JOINT BOOKRUNNERS\par \par       Barclays Bank PLC             Citigroup Global          Credit Suisse Securities           VTB Capital plc\par     5 The North Colonnade           Markets Limited               (Europe) Limited                 14 Cornhill\par         Canary Wharf                Citigroup  Centre       One Cabot Square \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 London E14 4QJ London EC3V 3ND\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2        London E14 4BB               33 Canada Square               United Kingdom                 United Kingdom\par        United Kingdom                 Canary Wharf\par                                      London E14 5LB\par                                      United Kingdom\par \par \par                           FISCAL AGENT AND REGISTRAR\par                         Citibank, N.A., London Branch\par                            