\par\par \b \uc2 Russian rouble's rally stalls near recent highs\b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rouble's rally pauses near 14-mth highs vs basket\par \par \uc2 * External factors remain supportive, market eyes oil\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 22 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble's rally stalled on Monday as oil and other high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  turned lower, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should still be supported by tax payments this week and relatively strong fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 In early trade, the rouble was down 3 kopecks against the euro-dollar basket at 33.97 <RUS=MCX>, still in sight of a 14-month high of 33.93 hit last Friday, according to Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 Downside pressure on the rouble reflects the oversold state of the local market, that has been already betting on the rouble's rise for almost two months.\par \par \uc2 "The appreciation has not paused yet, only excessive firming is on pause. Short positions (in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are preferred and are very big now. The weather is grey so the market is grey as well," said a dealer at a Russian bank.\par \par \uc2 The rouble showed rapid rises in the last seven weeks, supported by strong oil prices, exporters converting part of their revenues in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into roubles, and the appeal of carry trade \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the relatively big spread in interest rates compared to the U.S. or euro zone.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gradually cut rates since April 2009, bringing them to record lows, but with the benchmark refinancing rate at 8.50 percent -- higher than in all the other G8 states -- Russian assets retain their high-yielding status.\par \par \uc2 This appeal is set to remain even if the regulator slashes rates again this month, expectations for which were supported by lacklustre economic data last Friday [ID:nLDE62I1AZ].\par \par \uc2 The rouble may gain some support this week from tax payments in Russia -- value added tax payments are due on Monday and the tax on natural resources by March 25. The total tax payments will be close to 200-250 billion roubles ($6.8-$8.5 billion), according to Trust bank estimates.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, shifting the rouble's floating corridor by 5 kopecks for each $700 million of purchases at its boundary.\par \par \uc2 It has taken 22 such steps since mid-February, bringing the band to 33.90-36.90 against the basket on Friday, dealers said. The new presumed boundary has yet to be tested.\par \par \uc2 The rouble's performance will heavily depend on oil prices but, generally, the upward trend remains intact.\par \par \uc2 "The rouble's exchange rate is still 17 percent lower than pre-crisis levels, so the possibility of further appreciation is pretty high. Our view on the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains positive," analysts at Uralsib bank said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 By 0825 GMT, the rouble was down around 5 kopecks against the dollar at 29.33 <RUBUTSTN=MCX>. Versus the euro <EURRUBTN=MCX>, the rouble climbed to a fresh 15-month maximum of 39.5945, as the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under broad pressure on ongoing concerns over aid to debt-burdened Greece [FRX/]. (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh, editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100322e63m000hk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
