\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Greek woes weigh; Russia rouble rises\b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2010\par 13:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Emerging markets dip Greece overshadows Bernanke comments\par \par \uc2 * Turkish shares snap losing streak but lira weaker\par \par \uc2 * Rouble hits 14-month high; Serb dinar to test new low\par \par \uc2 By Sebastian Tong\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 25 (Reuters) - Mounting concerns over Greece's financial health weighed on emerging markets on Thursday though the U.S. Federal Reserve's pledge to keep interest rates exceptionally low for an extended period provided investors some comfort. Turkish shares <.XU100> broke a three-day losing streak sparked off by a probe into an alleged coup plot that heightened tensions between its secularist military and Islamist-rooted government while Russia rouble hit 14-month highs against its euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke's Wednesday affirmation that he would maintain loose monetary conditions sparked a rally that fizzled after stark warnings from rating agencies \uc2 Moody's\uc2  and \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  that Greek sovereign ratings were jeopardised by its inability to curb spending. [ID:nLDE61N2KL] [ID:nTOE61O07C]\par \par \uc2 Emerging shares <.MSCIEF>, which have underperformed world stocks <.MIWD00000PUS> since the start of the year, were 0.8 percent lower by 1145 GMT, while emerging sovereign debt spreads <11EMJ> widened two basis points to trade at 302 bps over U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 "Greece has overshadowed Bernanke's testimony to Congress and risk is on the back foot. The market is seeking some clarity on Greece - it's waiting for the sovereign bond issue and to see what the European Union will do about the situation," said Manik Narain, economist at Standard Chartered.\par \par \uc2 The sombre note sounded by the Fed chief on the U.S. economy also provided a sobering reminder of the fragility of the global recovery, Narain added.\par \par \uc2 "It's not just sovereign credit worthiness that is a worry but the state of the global economy."\par \par \uc2 Hungarian shares <.BUX> recovered 0.6 percent after sinking to a two-week low earlier in the day while Turkish shares rose over one percent after dropping some three percent to plumb 12-week lows in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 TURKEY; SERBIA\par \par \uc2 The lira pared losses against the dollar <TRY=> but languished near seven-month lows with investors continuing a close eye on developments on the unfolding investigation into an alleged plot by some Turkey's military officers to overthrow the government. [ID:nIST006632]\par \par \uc2 Five-year credit default swaps to insure Turkish sovereign debt were quoted unchanged at 197.5 bps from the previous day's close, according to CMA DataVision.\par \par \uc2 Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were broadly weaker with the Polish zloty backing further off from the 13-month highs reached on Tuesday <EURPLN=>.\par \par \uc2 Serbia's dinar <EURRSD=>, however, looked set to test the historic lows reached on Wednesday after its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said interest rates are likely to be cut rather than left unchanged. [ID:nLDE61O0WB]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to slow the unit's slide on Wednesday, blamed by local dealers on demand for euros from importers. [ID:nLDE61N23V]\par \par \uc2 However, analysts also say Greek fiscal woes could be a factor for Balkan economies such as Serbia.\par \par \uc2 "Bulgaria is the most exposed as Greece is one of the top-three export destinations (almost 10 percent of exports)... Greek foreign direct investments in Serbia are notable as well," said \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  in a client note.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but its move was sparked off by the strength of the rouble.\par \par \uc2 The rouble hit multi-month highs against its dual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket reinforced by healthy tax receipts and buoyant crude prices. [ID:nLDE61O0O4] (Reporting by Sebastian Tong; )\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100228e62p0009q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
