\par\par \b \uc2 Russia rouble hits 2010 high, eyes c.bank boundary\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2010\par 13:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Feb 16 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble hit its strongest level of the year on Tuesday, closing in on the current boundary of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's floating trading band thanks to higher oil prices and upcoming domestic tax payments.\par \par \uc2 The rouble firmed as far as 35.05 versus the euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX> -- just 5 kopecks away from the boundary of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current floating corridor of 35-38.\par \par \uc2 The rouble also firmed as far as 30.09 per dollar, its strongest in nearly two weeks <RUBUTSTN=MCX>. "Slowly but surely we are moving lower (in the basket/rouble rate)," said Mikhail Kulyk, dealer at \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2 , forecasting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's boundary could be reached "tomorrow if not today". As per its policy of smoothing out excessive exchange rate volatility, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the band's boundary before allowing the corridor to shift slightly.\par \par \uc2 In the past, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the band to shift by 5 kopecks for each $700 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This last happened in November 2009, but Kulyk said the parameters of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have likely remained unchanged since then.\par \par \uc2 Urals oil -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key export -- jumped over 2 percent to above $72 a barrel, or some $14 more than the average price for 2010 factored into the government budget <URL-E>.\par \par \uc2 "Some recovery in euro/dollar, as well as upward pressure on commodity prices could keep the rouble supported in the coming days," analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Also positive for the rouble are month-end domestic tax payments due next week, which analysts at Zenit estimated at around 370 billion roubles ($12.28 billion).\par \par \uc2 "Exporters are selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there will be a lot of payments coming up," said Kulyk, adding that companies were getting ready for the payments earlier than usual due to two days of public holidays at the start of next week. Nonetheless, not everyone expects the rouble's appreciation trend to prove long-lasting, with \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  recommending shorting the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the basket with a target of 36.50 "in anticipation of disappointing growth".\par \par \uc2 Markets have also turned slightly more negative on the rouble in the long term, with non-deliverable forwards showing it at 31.75 per dollar in a year's time -- over 50 kopecks weaker than at the end of last week, but still implying a fairly modest depreciation of around 5 percent <RUB1YNDFOR=>. (Writing by Toni Vorobyova; editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100216e62g000op\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
