\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russia rouble retrieves bulk of early week losses\b0\par\par\uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2009\par 13:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2  * Rouble regains 63 kopecks of early week losses\par \par \uc2  * Still remains 3.8 pct below mid-November highs\par \par \uc2  * Seen stable, slightly strengthening next week\par \par \uc2  By Lidia Kelly and Andrei Ostroukh\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Dec 11 (Reuters) -- Russia's rouble retrieved a big chunk of its early week losses by Friday-end, as crude prices started rising again and further signs of rebound in the global economy reinstated investors interest in riskier assets. The rouble closed at 36.45 against the dollar-euro basket <RUS=MCX> Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses for guiding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nominal exchange rate -- some 63 kopecks stronger than Wednesday's three-month low.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still traded weaker than last week's close of 35.98 and was 3.8 percent down from mid-November highs. But analysts said the improving sentiment across international markets should support the rouble in coming days.\par \par \uc2  "We expect the rouble to continue to appreciate slowly, heading toward the middle of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia's floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band (currently at 35-38 roubles against the basket0," Nikolai Podguzov, the head of fixed income strategy at Renaissance Capital in Moscow, said in a research note.\par \par \uc2  Oil prices reversed their week-long falling trend on Friday, [O/R] and Chinese data showed solid industrial growth, renewing confidence in emerging markets and their riskier, but higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "Next week might be a bit more optimistic than the beginning of this week," Artyom Arkhipov, chief market and macroeconomic analyst at Gazprombank, said.\par \par \uc2  "At the same time activity will be lower ahead of the New Year. We expect volatility to decrease and rouble could stabilize or strengthen modestly if oil prices don't fall below $70 (per barrel)."\par \par \uc2  Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been allowing much greater flexibility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate than previously, but it still guards carefully against high volatility, stepping in when it deems necessary to prevent excessive rouble fluctuations in either direction.\par \par \uc2  Some analysts suggest shorting the rouble at and above current levels around 30.00 per dollar, targeting a 27-28 roubles per dollar in the first quarter of next year <RUB=>, it is still a laggard versus other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, it does not appear outright hostile to a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and hard capital controls are unlikely," said \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  analysts.\par \par \uc2  The market at large believes the rouble should stay fairly stable in the next 12 months. Non-deliverable forwards (NDFs), which mirror investors' attitude towards \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , showed the rouble only slightly weaker in a year's time  at 31.85 per dollar --  compared to expectations for a 20 percent decline this time last year <RUB1YNDFOR=>.\par \par \uc2  (Writing by Lidia Kelly; Editing by Dmitry Sergeyev; Editing by Ron Askew) \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA/ROUBLE  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|P