\par\par \b \uc2 Russia's c.bank bought $7.3 bln in Nov\b0\par\par\uc2 119 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2009\par 15:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Dec 7 (Reuters) - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $7.3 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in November, the regulator said on its web site on Monday, half as much as in the previous month.\par \par \uc2 Of the total, so-called "planned" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which are usually carried out within the rouble's floating trading corridor, accounted for $2.9 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought a net 745 million euros, mostly through planned \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a net $15.2 billion and 485 million euros on the market.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Olga Borodina)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ROUBLE/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091210e5c70011u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
