\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Russian-French PM Meeting In Focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Marcin Sobczyk   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 1,360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2009\par 05:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par Local/GMT \par N/A       Russian Prime Minister Vladimir Putin meeting French counterpart \par           Francois Fillon in Paris. \par 1400/1300 New World Resources CFO Marek Jelinek online interview on Patria.cz. \par 1000/0900 Hungarian trade unions, employers continue 2010 wage talks. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--Market participants in Central and Eastern Europe Friday will be on the lookout for news from government talks between Russia and France, Hungarian negotiations between trade unions and employers, and comments from a Czech-based coal holding company that may shed light on regional energy developments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Russia's Vladimir Putin will meet France's Francois Fillon Friday, and the two prime ministers are expected to agree on the fate of indebted auto giant OAO \uc2 AvtoVAZ\uc2  (AVAZ.RS) in which France's Renault (RNO.FR) owns a 25% stake.\par \par \uc2 The Russian and French governments both have major stakes in their national car makers, and each have lent to them at discounted rates, but \uc2 AvtoVAZ\uc2  remains on the brink of bankruptcy.\par \par \uc2 Putin shocked investors in early autumn when he told his ministers that Renault's stake could be diluted unless the company puts up more funds for \uc2 AvtoVAZ\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, the Russian government's tone has since become more moderate, and Renault is expected to contribute to \uc2 AvtoVAZ\uc2 's bailout by handing over valuable technology, while the Russian government refinances \uc2 AvtoVAZ\uc2 's overdue debts.\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, wage talks between Hungarian trade unions and employers resume Friday after failing to yield results a week ago, despite the government's involvement. The National Alliance of Hungarian Trade Unions said Thursday that it won't support any proposal that would result in a decline in 2010 wages in real, or inflation-adjusted, terms. The government and the \uc2 National Bank of Hungary\uc2  forecast that inflation will average 3.9% next year.\par \par \uc2 In the Czech Republic, coal miner New World Resources (NWR.LN), which operates in the Czech Republic and Poland, may shed more light on its expectations on coal price developments in the remainder of 2009 and in 2010. NWR Chief Financial Officer Marek Jelinek will be answering questions in an online interview Friday held on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.patria.cz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.patria.cz}}}\uc2  of Czech-Belgium brokerage Patria Finance.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                    2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 26.2920-20 26.3400-00 -0.18  26.3460 26.3240  -1.72 \par EUR/HUF 272.25-75  272.27-77  -0.01  272.75  272.27   +3.30 \par EUR/PLN 4.1590-40  4.1559-09  +0.07  4.1750  4.1510   +1.07 \par USD/RUB 29.323-33  29.237-47  +0.29  29.347  29.239   -3.94 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 No dramatic forint weakening is expected Friday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell Thursday along with the rest of the region. The euro-forint cross may climb toward the upper end of the HUF265-HUF275 range in which it's been trading since early August, Takarekbank said. If Western European and Asian stock markets return to the black, there's a good chance that the forint could slip below HUF270 against the euro again Monday, it added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish zloty is likely to continue to weaken on poor global sentiment, a trader said. The Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to weaken to 4.15 against the euro Friday and possibly to 4.20 after the weekend.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the U.S. markets reopening after the Thanksgiving holiday Thursday, some traders expect the Czech koruna to continue testing levels near or at 26.20 against the euro. "I expect that the koruna will stay above 26.00, with 26.200 still acting as support," Raiffeisenbank trader Ivo Prokop said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , "while higher \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  [by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ] within the ruble's floating corridor might indeed increase volatility, the likelihood of the ruble hitting the strongest end of the floating range remains high," VTB Capital said. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  First Deputy Chairman Alexei Ulyukayev has said that the floating corridor is now RUB35-RUB38 against the basket of dollars and euros. A fall in oil prices Thursday put pressure on the Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but most economists expect it to keep appreciating on the back of foreign capital inflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARIAN BOND YIELDS - The three-year bond yield was at at 6.85%, flat from Wednesday afternoon. The five-year was at 7.13% from 7.10% and the 10-year at 7.42% from 7.40%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The "Dubai story may continue Friday," preventing Hungarian bonds from recovering, a trader said. "We will go into that direction, where the global sentiment takes us," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 News Wednesday that Dubai World, a holding company for the Dubai government, had requested a delay in repayment on about $35 billion of its debt shocked financial markets around the world, prompting a swift move out of risky asset markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLISH BOND YIELDS - The average yield on two-year treasury bonds was at 4.91% late Thursday from 4.90% late Wednesday; the five-year was at 5.65% from 5.63%; and 10-year was at 6.15% from 6.12%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish fixed-income market is stabilizing ahead of the holiday season with thin trading and limited volatility expected, a trader said. On Thursday, Polish bond yields were only slightly higher in very thin trade, with limited reaction to Thursday's switch tender of treasury bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH BOND YIELD - The yield on the benchmark 10-year paper eased to 4.12% late Thursday from 4.19% late Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG20                    2331.34  loss   34.10   dn 1.4% \par BUX                     20160.87  loss  513.19   dn 2.5% \par PX                       1103.50  loss   24.50   dn 2.2% \par RTS                      1366.85  loss   63.31   dn 4.4% \par Micex                    1268.92  loss   43.15   dn 3.3% \par DJ STOXX EU Enlarged 15  2131.25  loss   89.14   dn 4.0% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN WARSAW: Warsaw stocks are set to follow the U.S. markets and their reaction to the news on Dubai's credit woes when the U.S. markets reopen on Friday, a trader said. On Thursday, the Polish market mirrored poor global sentiment caused by the news from Dubai.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN PRAGUE: Czech stocks will remain driven by sentiment on core markets and are likely get their cue from the re-opening of the U.S. market after the Thanksgiving holiday, a local trader said. Amid shallow trading, most blue chips closed lower Thursday except for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telefonica O2 CR\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the only winner among the more actively traded stocks Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN BUDAPEST: Markets, including the Budapest Stock Exchange, have run out of steam and the Dubai World news just serves an excuse to sell, an Erste Bank trader said. "Markets have gained a lot and whether we'll start a downward trend is not clear yet," the traded added. "Since U.S. markets will still be [partially] closed, I wouldn't attach much significance to anything that happens on the market."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN MOSCOW: "If the dollar continues to slide then the [Russian] market will recover," said Veles Capital, after MICEX fell 3.3% with weaker crude prices and the fallout from Dubai World's debt problems.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Marcin Sobczyk, Dow Jones Newswires; +48 22 447 2432, marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Leos Rousek in Prague, Margit Feher in Budapest, Will Bland and Alexander Kolyandr in Moscow contributed to this article.) [ 11-26-09 2356ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland and Russia have yet to iron out the details of the planned natural gas agreement between its gas companies, Poland's Deputy Economy Minister Joanna Strzelec-Lobodzinska and Russia's Deputy Energy Minister Anatoly Yanovsky told a press conference on Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's consolidated budget deficit expanded to 25.5 billion lei ($9 billion) after the first ten months, amounting to 5.1% of the gross domestic product, Finance Ministry data showed Thursday, news agency Mediafax reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asseco Poland\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ACP.WA), Poland's largest home-grown software firm, has signed an agreement to buy 95% of shares in ZUI Orago, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asseco Poland\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a statement Thursday. [ 11-26-09 2356ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091127e5br00037\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
