\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russia eyes new measures to cap rouble rally\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2009\par 10:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rouble hits highest since Jan vs \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket\par \par \uc2 * Russia may consider soft measures to stem inflows\par \par \uc2 * C.bank chief reiterates he is against capital controls\par \par \uc2 (Recasts with Ignatyev comments)\par \par \uc2 By Yelena Fabrichnaya and Andrei Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 18 (Reuters) - Russia allowed the rouble to scale fresh, oil-fuelled highs versus a euro-dollar basket on Wednesday, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would consider "soft" measures to limit future speculative inflows into the country.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has firmed 9 percent versus the basket since September to 35.03, its strongest since January <RUS=MCX> as investors regain confidence in emerging markets, the domestic economy starts to recover from recession and oil prices hold near one-year highs <URL-E>.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so far \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to slow down the appreciation rather than stop it, but there are some signs officials are getting concerned about the inflow of hot money.\par \par \uc2 "I am against resuming capital control measures. At the same time, there are other measures, softer ones, which could slow down the inflow of speculative capital...It is being discussed," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Sergei Ignatyev told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Such measures could include monitoring external borrowing of state-controlled companies, as well as re-introducing differentiated minimum reserve requirements for banks' liabilities in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus those in the rouble, he added.\par \par \uc2 Currently the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the rouble's floating corridor to shift by 5 kopecks for each $700 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at either of the band's boundaries. Dealers say the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level is at 35.00 against the basket.\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev said earlier on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $6 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Nov. 1 and Nov. 17, after purchases of over $15 billion last month.\par \par \uc2 "The order of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may change ... It is possible that the floating (rouble) corridor could be altered not just automatically," Ignatyev told reporters later.\par \par \uc2 However he reiterated Russia's long-term goal remains to move to a floating exchange rate and inflation targeting.\par \par \uc2 "By my estimates it will take 1-1/2 years, possibly 2. And possibly it will not be an absolutely clean float," he said.\par \par \uc2 Officials have previously said \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  intends to reserve the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if it deems necessary even after the free float.\par \par \uc2 Another factor that could discourage capital inflows and cap the rouble's rally would be further interest rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 Ignatyev reiterated the likelihood of more monetary easing to come, saying the benchmark refinancing rate could be cut to under annualised 9.00 percent next year from 9.50 percent currently.\par \par \uc2 The minimum one-day repo rate, now at 6.75 percent, will be reduced more slowly than the refi, he added. The daily repo auctions have been the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's chief tool for providing short-term liquidity to the banking sector.\par \par \uc2 Russia saw a net capital outflow of $53 billion in the first 10 months of 2009, Ignatyev told parliament earlier. Based on previously reported data, that implies capital inflows of over $9 billion in October, in line with previous estimates. (Writing by Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091118e5bi000ic\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
