\par\par \b \uc2 Russia c.bank shifts bid level, buys $700 mln-dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2009\par 08:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday shifted its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid level after buying $700 million on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the appreciation of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moderate, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 In the second such move this week, the regulator moved its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid level to 35.00 roubles per euro/dollar basket <RUS=MCX>, used for guiding the rouble's nominal exchange rate policy, from the previous 35.05, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 At 0750 GMT, the rouble traded at 35.03 against the basket, 5 kopecks stronger than Tuesday's close at 35.08.\par \par \uc2 Monthly tax payments due in the coming days have added to the appreciating pressures on the rouble, a dealer from a foreign bank said in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 "It's possible that we will test another bid level, but I don't think we'll cross it," the dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has firmed by nearly 9 percent against the basket since its rally began in early September, recovering half of its losses incurred during a gradual depreciation a year ago.\par \par \uc2 Strong oil prices and global weakening of the dollar are supporting the rouble's rally, forcing systematic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts its bid for each $700 million in purchases. (Reporting by Andrei Ostroukh; writing by Lidia Kelly)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA/ROUBLE (URGENT)|LAN