\par\par \b \uc2 Russia c.bank shifts bid level to 35.05 rbl-dealers\b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2009\par 09:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifted on Monday its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid level at which it purchases foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market, local dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The regulator changed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid level to 35.05 roubles per euro/dollar basket <RUS=MCX>, used for guiding the rouble's nominal exchange rate policy, from the previous 35.10, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Usually, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts its bid for each $700 million in purchases, but on Monday it administered the move at trading volumes still below that amount.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been more forthcoming lately in revealing its market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policy plans, but it still does not comment on regular basis on its actions.\par \par \uc2 A dealer at a large Western bank in Moscow said the regulator might have shifted its bid level late last week, but because of the slight correction in the rouble that followed, the new bid had not been tested until now.\par \par \uc2 "There are no buyers," the dealer said. "Situation on the global markets remains optimistic."\par \par \uc2 At 0745 GMT, the rouble traded at 35.08 against the basket, 12 kopecks stronger from Friday's close at 35.20.\par \par \uc2 The rouble's recent strong recovery has been driven chiefly by improving external economic conditions, rising oil prices and subsequent influx of hot money from investors seeking high yields from short-term carry trade deals.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has firmed nearly 9 percent against the basket since its rally began in early September, recovering half of its losses incurred during gradual depreciation a year ago.\par \par \uc2 The rouble continues also to regain strength against the globally weakening dollar, trading early on Monday at 28.65, the strongest since December 2008. (Reporting by Andrei Ostroukh; writing by Lidia Kelly, editing by Mike Peacock)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA/ROUBLE|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091116e5bg000v0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
