\par\par \b \uc2 Russian markets -- Factors to Watch on Nov 10\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2009\par 08:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 10 (Reuters) - Here are events and news stories that could move Russian markets on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 You can reach us on: +7 495 775 1242\par \par \uc2 STOCKS CALL (Contributions to moscow.newsroom@reuters.com):\par \par \uc2 Uralsib: U.S. futures are trading slightly down, and Asian markets are up by around 0.5 percent this morning. Oil is somewhat weak at a few points below $80/bbl, and we expect the Russian market to open up 0.3-0.5 percent this morning.\par \par \uc2 OTP Bank\uc2 : We expect the market to open in the positive territory helped by growth in U.S. and Asian indexes, although slightly lower prices for oil and U.S. futures will be deterrents for Russian stocks.\par \par \uc2 EVENTS [RU-DIA] (All times GMT):\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - The World Bank's press conference on its latest report on Russia's economy. 0900.\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Austrian Chancellor Werner Faymann to meet Russian President Dmitry Medvedev and Prime Minister Vladimir Putin.\par \par \uc2 TOGLIATTI - First Deputy Prime Minister Igor Shuvalov to hold a meeting on troubled Russian car maker \uc2 AvtoVAZ\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Russian Natural Resources Minister Yuri Trutnev to chair a meeting of EU-Russia Permanent Partnership Council.\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold an auction for five-week collateral-free loans for commercial banks, with 15 billion roubles on offer at a minimum bid rate of 11.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW - International Industry Forum of Russia, CIS, the Baltics and Eastern Europe entitled 'Metal Expo 2009'\par \par \uc2 IN THE PAPERS [PRESS/RU]:\par \par \uc2 Russian broadcaster CTC Media has filed lawsuits against its board member and former CEO Alexander Rodnyansky, seeking to deprive him of his rights to exercise share options which could fetch him up to $100 million, Vedomosti writes.\par \par \uc2 TOP STORIES IN RUSSIA AND THE CIS [RU-NEWS]: COMPANIES/MARKETS: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rouble strengthens, c.bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     [ID:nL9451088]\par *\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PM backs \f28 \uc2 \f2 Siemens\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rosatom\f28 \uc2 \f2  nuclear pact   [ID:nL9482974]\par *Mechel returns to profit in Q2                  [ID:nL9105636]\par *\f28 \uc2 \f2 Rostelecom\f28 \uc2 \f2  H1 earnings fall 85 pct              [ID:nL9361342]\par  \par  \par  ECONOMY/POLITICS:\par *Russia c.bank may cut rates again, buy gold     [ID:nL9384036]\par *Russia car sales down 52 pct in Oct - AEB       [ID:nL9407289]\par *\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should limit \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -IMF        [ID:nL9464536]\par  \par  \par  ENERGY:\par *Europe deals, high costs sour \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  outlook   [ID:nL9362196]\par *Sistema eyes oil firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russneft\f28 \uc2 \f2  - paper          [ID:nL9363663]\par *LUKOIL gets $300 mln loan from EBRD             [ID:nL0427155]\par  \par  \par  COMMODITIES:\par *Russia grain up on export demand, govt buys     [ID:nL9383640]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Russia winter grain area seen record since 1992 [ID:nL9412004]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKETS CLOSE/LATEST:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  RTS                   <.IRTS>           1,409.9   +0.16 pct\par  MSCI Russia           <.MIRU00000PUS>     805.2   +5.73 pct\par  MSCI Emerging Markets <.MSCIEF>           962.6   +0.30 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia 30-year Eurobond<RU011428878=> yield: 5.507/5.464 pct\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EMBI+ Russia <11EM