\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Investors Monitor Drama In Latvia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2009\par 05:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Go to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/new-europe}}}\uc2  for the new Dow Jones blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Marek Strzelecki and Malgorzata Halaba \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par Local/GMT \par 0900/0700 Hungarian August trade data \par 0900/0700 Czech September jobless rate \par 1000/0800 Poland's Finance Ministry, IMF present regional economic outlook \par 1200/1000 Hungarian 2013/E T-Bond tender \par 1200/1000 Hungarian 2015/A T-Bond tender \par 1200/1000 Hungarian 2019/A T-Bond tender \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 WARSAW (Dow Jones)--Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equities markets will follow the investment mood as concerns emerge again about the economic situation in Latvia.\par \par \uc2 In a statement Wednesday, Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said confidence in local economy and financial system was waning due to concern over the state budget and a proposal to limit the liability of borrowers toward lenders to the value of collateral - a measure that could hurt local banks.\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, August trade figures are likely to show that a recovery in the export-driven economy is still a long way off, as earlier-released industrial output data were disappointing.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par        Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                   2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 25.6970-70 25.7070-70 -0.04  25.7280 25.6970  -3.95 \par EUR/HUF 269.37-52  269.18-47  +0.07  269.42  269.42   +2.21 \par EUR/PLN 4.2175-25  4.2222-42  -0.11  4.2212  4.2195   +2.49 \par USD/RUB 29.667-73  29.741-46  -0.25  29.785  29.654   -2.81 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint is expected to remain Thursday close to its current level of HUF269 to the euro, a dealer said. The forint eased Wednesday with other central and Eastern European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the news about a possible devaluation of the Latvian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . In the coming days, the forint will likely trade between HUF266-HUF270 to the euro, the trader added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish zloty is likely to head toward PLN4.25 to the euro following Wednesday's slide, traders said, citing the deteriorating situation in Latvia, which is raising fears of the lat devaluation. In Poland, a government reshuffle - and thus political uncertainty - will not help the zloty either.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Czech koruna is likely to remain under selling pressure Thursday, as investors are seen switching funds to the zloty. "Expectations of further monetary policy easing and even an outright \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will also further affect the koruna," a local trader said. The koruna is seen testing levels above CZK25.70 to CZK25.75 against the euro, some traders added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market participants expect further strengthening of the ruble against the dollar. "External factors argue in favor of further weakening of the dollar, supporting market participants' expectations of further ruble strengthening," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alfa Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a note. The Russian ruble fell against the basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but remained almost flat against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARIAN BOND YIELDS - The average three-year benchmark yield was at 7.29% late Wednesday from 7.10% late Tuesday, five-year was unchanged at 7.50%, and the 10-year was at 7.85% from 7.80%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian bond market will eye Thursday's treasury bond auction after a slight weakening Wednesday, a trader said. The weakening was partly a result of a regional market slump because of negative news from Latvia about a possible devaluation of the Latvian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLISH BOND YIELDS - The average yield on the two-year paper was at 5.11% late Wednesday from 5.10% late Tuesday, the five-year was unchanged at 5.71%, and the yield on the 10-year was at 6.21% from 6.20%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Polish bonds may weaken Thursday following the zloty's slide, which was shrugged off Wednesday due to the successful auction of a two-year T-Bond, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH BOND YIELD - The yield on the benchmark 10-year paper was at 4.72% late Wednesday, compared with 4.80% Tuesday afternoon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EQUITIES \par  \par WIG20                   2183.16  loss   39.11  dn 1.8% \par BUX                    20048.68  loss  237.36  dn 1.2% \par PX                      1134.2   loss   10.00  dn 0.9% \par RTS                     1287.37  gain   16.74  up 1.3% \par Stoxx EU Enlarged 15   2112.68   loss   42.77  dn 2% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN WARSAW: The WIG20 is likely to continue its slide Thursday after resistance at 2200 proved to be too strong, brokers said, adding that the market testing 2160 is likely. A local broker added that the market was dragged down by \f28 \uc2 \f2 PKO Bank Polski\f28 \uc2 \f2 , because its rights to new shares began trading Wednesday. "This always causes huge supply of rights by shareholders who are not interested in new shares and want to cash the rights as soon as possible," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN PRAGUE: Czech stocks will take their cue from moves on major markets in Europe Thursday. "Unless core markets rebound, local blue chips may face more sell offs," a local trader said. On Wednesday, driven largely by CEZ, which closed down 2%, Czech stocks succumbed to profit-taking pressures and closed lower.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN BUDAPEST: Hungarian stocks will likely watch the U.S. for direction Thursday. Aluminum giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alcoa\f28 \uc2 \f2  unofficially kicks off the earnings season with its results, which are expected to affect Far Eastern markets that in turn will have a knock-on effect on Hungarian stocks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN MOSCOW: "Valuation discount to global peers, low bond yields and high oil price remain Russia's key upside drivers", said a Moscow-based trader. The RTS closed 1.3% higher at a new year-high of 1287.37, led by oil and banking stocks, on strong oil prices and expectations of further depreciation of the dollar.. [ 10-07-09 2339ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  OTHER NEWS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUSSIA: Russia will not reduce its gas exports to Ukraine next year or change its contract conditions, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom OAO\f28 \uc2 \f2 's chief executive said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUSSIA: Russia's largest carmaker \f28 \uc2 \f2 AvtoVAZ\f28 \uc2 \f2  produced 29,846 vehicles in September, down 44.7% on the year, the press service of the Samara Region's governor said Wednesday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 AvtoVAZ\f28 \uc2 \f2  produced 220,986 vehicles in January-September. The company's sales fell 43.5% on the year in January-September.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 RUSSIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to launch a limited grain \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buying program within the next couple of weeks, targeting specific regions where grains are difficult to export from, Chris Vanhonacker, commercial director of RIAS Trading SA, told Dow Jones Newswires Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's liberal Prime Minister Donald Tusk on Wednesday announced a cabinet reshuffle in the wake of a graft scandal which led to dismissals of the interior and justice ministers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: European Union leaders on Wednesday warned the Czech Republic of the costs of further delaying the E.U. reform treaty as the euroskeptic Czech president holds out against the pact.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Three-fourths of Hungarians speak no language other than their own, according to Wednesday's national daily Nepszabadsag, citing a Eurostat survey of 25 to 64 year olds in the 27 European Union countries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: It could help solve the European Union's dairy market problems if Hungary's proposals were - partly or wholly - accepted, farming minister Jozsef Graf said in Budapest on Wednesday. EU agricultural ministers will discuss ways to tackle the milk market problems later in the month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: The Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday pumped 15 billion lei ($5.17 billion) into the money market in two repurchase agreement \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , after an earlier \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week failed to support market liquidity, news agency Mediafax reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BULGARIA: Bulgaria is likely to postpone its first step to joining the euro zone until early 2010, Finance Minister Simeon Djankov said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Marek Strzelecki, Dow Jones Newswires; +4822 447-2433; marek.strzelecki@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Alexander Kolyandr in Moscow, Leos Rousek in Prague, and Veronika Gulyas in Budapest contributed to this article.) [ 10-07-09 2339ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091008e5a80000n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
