\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  rouble firm, dealers cite more  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2009\par 16:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 28 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble started the week on a firm note, with dealers saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued small-scale dollar purchases for a third day on Monday in a bid to keep a lid on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Investors have turned more positive on the rouble of late thanks to brightening economic prospects and comparatively high interest rates. In the short term, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also got a boost from month- and quarter-end tax payments.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the rouble breached the psychologically key 30 mark to the dollar for the first time since January, and hit four-month peaks versus a bi-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket <RUS=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, it closed 30.1040 per dollar <RUBUTSTN=MCX> and 36.3957 against the basket -- slightly firmer on the day and in sight of the recent peaks.\par \par \uc2 The rally has prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come out with dollar purchases for the first time since June as part of its policy to avoid large exchange rate swings in either direction.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the 36.40 mark against the basket for a third trading day, but the scale of its actions remained modest.\par \par \uc2 Sergei Romanchuk, dealer at Metallinvestbank, estimated Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $100-200 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may well continue to buy dollars on Tuesday, he said, as the rouble remains firm despite a retreat in oil prices <URL-E>.\par \par \uc2 "The market does not believe that oil prices can continue to fall," he said.\par \par \uc2 In a sign of increasingly positive sentiment on Russia, KBC Securities on Monday forecast rouble gains versus the euro and suggested these could be played by buying Russian stocks. (Reporting by Andrei Ostroukh; Writing by Toni Vorobyova; Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090928e59s000zp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
