\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE: IMF Urges Russia To Act On Banks, Redirect Stimulus\b0\par\par\uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2009\par 16:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Adds details of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  interest rate cut.) \par  \par    By Andrew Langley and Will Bland \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--Russia should take a more hands-on approach to tackling problems in its banking sector and redirect its stimulus package toward more temporary spending in order to build on early signs of an economic recovery, the International Monetary Fund said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The IMF - which sees the Russian economy shrinking 6.5% in 2009 - also welcomed recent interest rate cuts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but warned against being too aggressive in easing monetary policy further amid volatility in the ruble exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "Banks' financial situation and loan portfolios are now deteriorating at a notably faster pace. The key immediate challenge facing the authorities at this time is how to deal with these mounting problems," the IMF's executive board wrote in an annual report.\par \par \uc2 It said Russia should be more "proactive" in addressing the issues affecting the sector to avoid a prolonged credit freeze, advising the authorities to recapitalize struggling lenders, stress-test the largest institutions and beef up the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's supervisory powers, in part to better understand thus-far opaque asset quality.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday cut rates for the fifth time since April, but acknowledged that private banks are still reluctant to lend, and said this is delaying a revival of the country's economy.\par \par \uc2 The 25-basis-point cut was smaller than the previous ones and reflected concerns over faster-than-expected consumer price inflation in July of 0.6%.\par \par \uc2 The IMF statement said the lower lending rates will eventually filter through to the real economy, but that the country needs to make structural changes to get banks to lend the funds on.\par \par \uc2 "Absent a more determined policy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there is a risk that banks will continue to struggle to adjust balance sheets, stifling credit expansion and impeding a recovery," the IMF said.\par \par \uc2 Battered by lower commodity prices and scant access to credit, Russia's economy shrank more than 10% on the year between January and June. Gross domestic product will fall 8.5% for the whole 2009, according to the latest government forecasts.\par \par \uc2 But recent reports on manufacturing and rail cargo suggest that the worst of Russia's first recession in a decade has now passed and that the second half of the year will be better.\par \par \uc2 "The latest data...provide tentative signs that the economy may have recently reached a turning point," the IMF said.\par \par \uc2 But it warned that growth in 2010 will be slow, while the focus of the government's current stimulus program could endanger future economic expansion.\par \par \uc2 "A better-targeted yet smaller stimulus could have a similar impact on economic activity...but would reduce the risk of causing a permanent change in the tax and expenditure structure," the IMF said. "[The IMF] recommends reorienting the stimulus toward a temporary increase in social transfers targeted on credit-constrained households, and suggests a front-loading of infrastructure projects for which preparations are advanced alongside a strengthening of procurement procedures."\par \par \uc2 On the ruble, the IMF said \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on a temporary basis if rates become unsettled.\par \par \uc2 It said that the rates should be flexible but that the current exchange rate "remains broadly in equilibrium."\par \par \uc2 A Russian Finance Ministry spokesman declined to comment on the report immediately, saying that the ministry hasn't had time to review it fully. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Fund Web site: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.imf.org"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.imf.org}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Langley and Will Bland, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 937 8445; andrew.langley@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 07, 2009 10:42 ET (14:42 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090807e587004l0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
