\par\par \b \uc2 Rouble slips to 2-mth lows, c.bank stays away\b0\par\par\uc2 By Toni Vorobyova   \par \uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2009\par 15:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, July 9 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble slipped to 2-month lows versus a euro-dollar basket on Thursday on the back of this week's retreat in oil prices, but dealers said the fall was not steep enough to prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rouble snapped a four-month long winning streak -- fuelled by gains in oil and domestic stocks -- in late June. It weakened as far as 37.57 versus the euro-dollar basket <RUS=MCX>, before closing down 0.24 percent on the day at 37.51.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which spent $200 billion to avoid a rouble collapse in late 2008-early 2009, stayed away.\par \par \uc2 "It (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is not there," said a dealer at a European bank. "I think it will have to come out if there is a really sharp move in the rouble, say 2 roubles (in one day)."\par \par \uc2 Urals oil traded around $60 per barrel <URL-E> after dipping below that mark for the first time since late May on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "Although in the next months the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to feel the support of improved capital flows and a positive current account, the technical weakening trend in oil prices suggests short-term downside risks for the rouble," ING analyst Stanislav Ponomarenko said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 "We also remain cautious on the prospects of the rouble in the longer term taking into account the likely continuing combination of the weakness of the real economy and relatively high inflation."\par \par \uc2 Thursday brought more bad news on the economy, with Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin saying the 2010 budget deficit could be as high as 7.5 percent [ID:nL9441446]. However there was also some rouble-positive news in the form of a higher May trade surplus thanks to rising exports and falling imports [ID:nMOS005473].\par \par \uc2 Versus the dollar the rouble hit 7-week lows but stopped short of weakening beyond the 32 mark <RUB=>. Another key level for investors is 38 roubles to the basket.\par \par \uc2 "Above the 38 mark in the basket-rouble exchange rate things are beginning to get dangerous," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "The memory of the recent collapse of the rouble is still very present so that depreciation expectations could easily lead to a spiral of rouble sales. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would however be able to prevent this with the help of early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves stood at $409 billion as of July 3, data showed on Thursday [ID:nMOS005472].\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA-ROUBLE/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090709e5790010o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
